        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_35-2.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verf. vermengt ‘Ungehorsam’ mit ‘Königsschutz’, beides als Strafgeldfixa (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13. 16) erkennend—<hi rend="italic">griðb</hi>.{21}—<hi rend="italic">burchb</hi>.{24}, emendiere <hi rend="italic">borgb</hi>.—{29}<hi rend="italic">culpam</hi> fehlt—<hi rend="italic">q. per pers</hi>.—36. <hi rend="italic">Item</hi>.{27} <hi rend="italic">Qui</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The author confuses ‘disobedience’ with ‘king’s protection’, recognizing both as fixed fines (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13. 16)—<hi rend="italic">griðb</hi>.{21}—<hi rend="italic">burchb</hi>.{24}, emend to <hi rend="italic">borgb</hi>.—{29}<hi rend="italic">culpam</hi> missing—<hi rend="italic">q. per pers</hi>.—36. <hi rend="italic">Item</hi>.{27} <hi rend="italic">Qui</hi> Rs</seg></note>
